# TCS Digital Project Roadmaps
**Simplified Full-Stack Architecture & File Structure (No JWT Overhead)**  
**Tech Stack:** Python | FastAPI | Streamlit | MySQL | SQLite | Pydantic

---

## 1. Simplified Architecture & File Structure
To keep development fast, clean, and easy to explain in an interview, both projects use a flat 4-file repository structure without authentication boilerplate. Every technology in your stack has a clear, practical responsibility:

| Technology | Role in the Application |
| :--- | :--- |
| **FastAPI** | Serves as the decoupled REST API backend with built-in Swagger UI testing (`/docs`). |
| **Pydantic** | Validates incoming JSON payloads (data types, positive numbers, allowed categories) before DB writes. |
| **MySQL** | Primary relational database storing persistent core business records (Expenses or Support Tickets). |
| **SQLite** | Lightweight local storage for fast activity audit logs or instant FAQ self-help lookups. |
| **Streamlit** | Interactive Python frontend consuming the FastAPI endpoints via HTTP requests. |

### Standard GitHub Folder Structure (Applies to Both Projects)
```text
project-root/
├── backend.py        # FastAPI app, SQLAlchemy engines (MySQL + SQLite), Pydantic schemas & routes
├── frontend.py       # Single-page Streamlit dashboard consuming FastAPI endpoints
├── .env              # MySQL connection URL and SQLite file path
├── requirements.txt  # Project dependencies (fastapi, uvicorn, sqlalchemy, pymysql, streamlit, etc.)
└── README.md         # Project overview, architecture explanation & run instructions
```

